    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"Edgecase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.layout_spiral - Edgecase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"Edgecase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.layout_spiral.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.layout_spiral()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | Edgecase\n  description: Place the nodes along a spiral, in ID order.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.layout_spiral()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | Edgecase\n  description: Place the nodes along a spiral, in ID order.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.layout_spiral()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Place the nodes along a spiral, in ID order.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nPlace the nodes along a spiral, in ID order.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L5129-L5226){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.layout_spiral(\n    resolution=0.35,\n    equidistant=False,\n    scale=1.0,\n    center=(0.0, 0.0),\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Spiral layout](../assets/graphs/layout-spiral.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"On the left, a path of nine nodes scattered at random. On the right, layout_spiral(1.4, equidistant=True) sets the nodes evenly spaced along a spiral in id order, so the path curls around half a turn; a faint line traces the spiral on in to its center.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nBy default node `i` (counting from `0`) goes at distance `i` from the center and angle\n`resolution * i`, an Archimedean spiral whose turns get farther apart in arc length as\nit grows. With `equidistant=True` consecutive nodes are instead one unit apart along\nthe curve, so the spacing stays even all the way out. The spiral is then centered and\nscaled so the farthest coordinate is `scale=`. Edges play no part, so like\n`layout_circular()` the picture shows node order; a spiral packs long sequences\n(time-ordered events, paths) more compactly than a circle. This matches NetworkX's\n`spiral_layout()`.\n\nPositions are stored as `[x, y]` lists in the `attr_name=` node attribute; see\n`layout_circular()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[resolution]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[0.35]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Angle step between consecutive nodes, in radians: smaller values give a tighter,\n    more compact spiral. With `equidistant=True` it sets where the spiral starts\n    instead: at angle `resolution + 2 / resolution`, which is closest to the center\n    near `1.4`. Default is `0.35`.\n\n<code>[equidistant]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, space consecutive nodes evenly along the spiral. Default is `False`.\n\n<code>[scale]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[1.0]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Largest coordinate after rescaling. Default is `1.0`.\n\n<code>[center]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [tuple[float, float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [(0.0, 0.0)]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Center of the layout, as `(x, y)`. Default is the origin.\n\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Node attribute to store the positions in. If `None` (default), uses `\"pos\"`.\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns a dictionary instead of self. If `False` (default), stores the\n    positions on the nodes and returns self for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Union[dict[int, tuple[float, float]], Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: dictionary mapping node IDs to `(x, y)` tuples. If\n    `return_dict=` is `False` (default): returns self for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `resolution=` is not a positive number, or `scale=` or `center=` is invalid.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA path of 40 nodes wound into a spiral:\n\n::: {#745bd684 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nec.Graph().add_path_graph(40).layout_spiral(equidistant=True).plot(layout=\"pos\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"8.4 16.0 683.3 488.1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"8.4\" y=\"16.0\" width=\"683.3\" height=\"488.1\" fill=\"#fafafa\"/>\n<line x1=\"350.4\" y1=\"439.2\" x2=\"347.9\" y2=\"439.3\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<line x1=\"350.4\" y1=\"439.2\" x2=\"347.9\" y2=\"439.3\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"transparent\" stroke-width=\"8.0\" pointer-events=\"stroke\" data-edge=\"22-21-0\" data-attrs='{\"id\": 21, \"edge\": \"21 \\u2014 22\"}'/>\n<line x1=\"378.0\" y1=\"435.4\" x2=\"380.4\" y2=\"434.8\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<line x1=\"378.0\" y1=\"435.4\" x2=\"380.4\" y2=\"434.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"transparent\" stroke-width=\"8.0\" pointer-events=\"stroke\" data-edge=\"22-23-1\" data-attrs='{\"id\": 22, \"edge\": \"22 \\u2014 23\"}'/>\n<line x1=\"408.5\" y1=\"218.5\" x2=\"409.4\" y2=\"220.5\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<line x1=\"408.5\" y1=\"218.5\" x2=\"409.4\" y2=\"220.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"transparent\" stroke-width=\"8.0\" pointer-events=\"stroke\" data-edge=\"3-2-2\" data-attrs='{\"id\": 2, \"edge\": \"2 \\u2014 3\"}'/>\n<line x1=\"393.7\" y1=\"195.1\" x2=\"392.2\" y2=\"193.4\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<line x1=\"393.7\" y1=\"195.1\" x2=\"392.2\" y2=\"193.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"transparent\" stroke-width=\"8.0\" pointer-events=\"stroke\" data-edge=\"3-4-3\" data-attrs='{\"id\": 3, \"edge\": \"3 \\u2014 4\"}'/>\n<line x1=\"435.9\" y1=\"410.5\" x2=\